00:57:06.870 --> 00:57:08.790
I just don't think there's a
lot of things you can do to

00:57:08.790 --> 00:57:11.790
creatively embarrass yourself, honestly.

00:57:11.790 --> 00:57:12.810
And in one sense,

00:57:12.810 --> 00:57:17.130
I think that gets into one
of the sort of unrealized

00:57:17.130 --> 00:57:20.850
motivations to do something like this is,

00:57:20.850 --> 00:57:23.616
you know me, I talk about it all the time,

00:57:23.616 --> 00:57:26.123
is that I do have this chip
on my shoulder creatively.

00:57:27.750 --> 00:57:31.170
There's lots of things that
we want to do collectively

00:57:31.170 --> 00:57:35.370
to show people what we
are capable of creatively.

00:57:35.370 --> 00:57:36.870
And I think there's always an element

00:57:36.870 --> 00:57:38.700
of that in everything that I do.

00:57:38.700 --> 00:57:40.320
And so I can't,

00:57:40.320 --> 00:57:41.670
I'm not gonna be dishonest with you

00:57:41.670 --> 00:57:45.735
and tell you that I believe

00:57:45.735 --> 00:57:46.568
in what I've created here.

00:57:46.568 --> 00:57:47.610
And I think it's good.

00:57:47.610 --> 00:57:49.443
And I think other people will agree.

00:57:50.520 --> 00:57:53.170
And there's a part of my
ego that wants you to agree.

00:57:54.480 --> 00:57:56.400
Okay, well then I've
struck your ego enough,

00:57:56.400 --> 00:57:59.190
but I also think I'm projecting, I guess,

00:57:59.190 --> 00:58:01.410
in that if I were in your
shoes, that's how I would feel.

00:58:01.410 --> 00:58:04.920
So instead, I think it's,

00:58:04.920 --> 00:58:09.920
it's something that's inspiring
about the fact that you have

00:58:12.870 --> 00:58:14.163
this confidence,

00:58:15.360 --> 00:58:17.160
maybe it comes from a chip
on your shoulder or whatever,

00:58:17.160 --> 00:58:18.930
but like, you want to express yourself

00:58:18.930 --> 00:58:20.880
in this way and you go for it.

00:58:20.880 --> 00:58:22.413
And that's something that,

00:58:23.970 --> 00:58:25.800
I could do more of.

00:58:25.800 --> 00:58:28.380
So if I am to make this
about me for a second,

00:58:28.380 --> 00:58:29.853
I do feel like,

00:58:31.554 --> 00:58:34.500
I would be embarrassed at every turn.

00:58:34.500 --> 00:58:37.050
Even the thing about talking
about like being a DJ,

00:58:37.050 --> 00:58:39.000
I had to make a decision to say,

00:58:39.000 --> 00:58:41.887
this is kind of a, this is not.

00:58:42.840 --> 00:58:44.500
I had to decide what my

00:58:48.450 --> 00:58:50.220
posture was gonna be about it.

00:58:50.220 --> 00:58:51.480
Right.

00:58:51.480 --> 00:58:52.313
It's like, yeah,

00:58:52.313 --> 00:58:53.860
this is something that I'm into

00:58:55.020 --> 00:58:56.280
and I'm not gonna be sheepish

00:58:56.280 --> 00:59:00.610
or apologetic or embarrassed
by having some sort

00:59:02.382 --> 00:59:04.443
of creative outlet or aspirations.

00:59:06.190 --> 00:59:07.470
So I think that's where that
question was coming from.

00:59:07.470 --> 00:59:09.450
It's more about me than you, but.

00:59:09.450 --> 00:59:11.157
No, but I have thought about it.

00:59:11.157 --> 00:59:14.520
The the worst case scenario is
people are like this YouTube

00:59:14.520 --> 00:59:19.230
guy thinks he's a musician now, who cares?

00:59:19.230 --> 00:59:20.063
Right.

00:59:20.063 --> 00:59:20.896
Okay.

00:59:20.896 --> 00:59:21.729
I've lost nothing.

00:59:22.800 --> 00:59:24.360
If you already see me as that,

00:59:24.360 --> 00:59:26.430
if you see me as this YouTube guy,

00:59:26.430 --> 00:59:30.870
this hack that just stumbled into fame

00:59:30.870 --> 00:59:33.120
and isn't really talented, then nothing.

00:59:33.120 --> 00:59:34.290
If you already think that,

00:59:34.290 --> 00:59:37.380
then you thinking that again
is not a problem for me.

00:59:37.380 --> 00:59:38.670
You know what I'm saying?

00:59:38.670 --> 00:59:39.503
Yeah.

00:59:44.071 --> 00:59:45.510
Is there bigger,

00:59:45.510 --> 00:59:49.830
there's bigger risks
content wise in other songs.

00:59:49.830 --> 00:59:52.080
Yeah, it gets more explicit, literally.

00:59:52.080 --> 00:59:54.333
There's a few FBOs dropped on the album,

00:59:57.738 --> 00:59:59.412
to give a hint of that.

00:59:59.412 --> 01:00:00.907
Are you nervous about any

01:00:00.907 --> 01:00:02.010
of the specifics coming out?

01:00:02.010 --> 01:00:02.843
I mean what.

01:00:02.843 --> 01:00:03.862
No.

01:00:03.862 --> 01:00:04.695
Where's.

01:00:04.695 --> 01:00:06.064
No, no.

01:00:06.064 --> 01:00:06.897
I mean you wrote a,

01:00:06.897 --> 01:00:08.130
you said you wrote a song to your kids.

01:00:08.130 --> 01:00:09.780
You wrote a song to your parents.

01:00:12.107 --> 01:00:12.940
Well, yeah,

01:00:15.990 --> 01:00:18.273
I don't know how much
I wanna talk about the.

01:00:19.889 --> 01:00:20.940
I have a great relationship
with my parents,

01:00:20.940 --> 01:00:22.740
but the thing that I am conscious of

01:00:24.123 --> 01:00:26.070
is that because they are still
very much strong Christians.

01:00:26.070 --> 01:00:27.780
and I'm very much a public figure

01:00:27.780 --> 01:00:30.180
who has stated that I am not,

01:00:30.180 --> 01:00:32.080
and that I'm critical of Christianity,

01:00:32.985 --> 01:00:34.320
that makes their life more difficult

01:00:34.320 --> 01:00:36.393
than I would like it to be, right?

01:00:37.860 --> 01:00:41.100
Because of the way people
in the church are, you know?

01:00:41.100 --> 01:00:42.960
And so, and just the way
people in general are,

01:00:42.960 --> 01:00:45.383
not to single a out the people
in the church, it's just.

01:00:46.387 --> 01:00:48.467
If somebody that you're related

01:00:48.467 --> 01:00:50.340
to is talking about what you're all into,

01:00:50.340 --> 01:00:52.590
then they become a little
bit of a scapegoat.

01:00:56.538 --> 01:00:58.008
And I'm sensitive to that

01:00:58.008 --> 01:00:58.980
and in some ways that's
kind of what the song

01:00:58.980 --> 01:00:59.943
to them is about.

01:01:00.990 --> 01:01:04.502
Well, we can leave that part at that.

01:01:04.502 --> 01:01:06.120
'Cause I do think I would like to,

01:01:06.120 --> 01:01:08.070
I'm gonna hear the whole
album at some point

01:01:08.070 --> 01:01:11.430
and then if we can kind of,
I'm sure we'll revisit this.

01:01:11.430 --> 01:01:12.693
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:01:12.693 --> 01:01:15.990
But you know, in terms of when
we started talking about it,

01:01:15.990 --> 01:01:18.690
I was trying to remember when
that was, do you remember?

01:01:18.690 --> 01:01:20.490
'Cause I think there were like hints

01:01:23.299 --> 01:01:25.110
of I'm writing some song,

01:01:25.110 --> 01:01:26.230
I'm writing some songs

01:01:27.074 --> 01:01:27.990
and I just remember the first time

01:01:27.990 --> 01:01:32.460
it kinda registered was
maybe you had mentioned it

01:01:32.460 --> 01:01:33.293
a few times,

01:01:33.293 --> 01:01:35.310
but you had mentioned it in an EP.

01:01:35.310 --> 01:01:39.720
I think that's the first
time I was like, what?

01:01:39.720 --> 01:01:40.553
Hmm.

01:01:41.700 --> 01:01:43.143
You're gonna, okay.

01:01:44.171 --> 01:01:45.977
So you're not just writing songs.

01:01:45.977 --> 01:01:49.023
You're gonna release songs, you know?

01:01:54.219 --> 01:01:55.052
What were you thinking there?

01:01:55.052 --> 01:01:57.060
Because again, it's like it,

01:01:57.060 --> 01:02:00.210
what you just told everybody

01:02:00.210 --> 01:02:03.450
for the past hour is not,

01:02:03.450 --> 01:02:06.540
was not the entry point
for our conversation.

01:02:06.540 --> 01:02:09.213
We never sat down and you said,

01:02:11.220 --> 01:02:14.400
hey, gave me this whole story.

01:02:14.400 --> 01:02:15.233
Hmm.

01:02:15.233 --> 01:02:17.493
So to me, my experience was,

01:02:18.360 --> 01:02:21.273
oh, he's doing this thing he
doesn't want to talk about,

01:02:22.329 --> 01:02:23.929
but then he feels like he needs,

01:02:24.960 --> 01:02:26.730
apparently it's gaining momentum

01:02:26.730 --> 01:02:28.250
'cause he's talking about making an EP.

01:02:28.250 --> 01:02:31.173
So now he's mentioning it
to me and I respect it.

01:02:31.173 --> 01:02:33.510
Like I have an appreciation for it now,

01:02:33.510 --> 01:02:35.117
given what you've said, that is like,

01:02:35.117 --> 01:02:38.403
it's a deeply personal
exercise that is an,

01:02:40.620 --> 01:02:45.360
an application of therapy that
then you would obviously talk

01:02:45.360 --> 01:02:46.893
to Jessie about,

01:02:47.760 --> 01:02:49.990
in the same way that
there's plenty of stuff

01:02:51.571 --> 01:02:54.213
in my personal journey, in my heart,

01:02:54.213 --> 01:02:58.260
in my therapy sessions that I
process myself, first of all.

01:02:58.260 --> 01:03:00.933
And then there's much of that,

01:03:03.450 --> 01:03:05.562
the vast majority of that,

01:03:05.562 --> 01:03:07.017
that I'll bring, that
Christie and I will discuss

01:03:07.017 --> 01:03:09.213
and I'll bring her into and then.

01:03:10.140 --> 01:03:12.840
So I recognize that then there's
certain things at certain

01:03:12.840 --> 01:03:15.300
times that I'll bring you into it.

01:03:15.300 --> 01:03:17.340
And it's not even a calculation

01:03:17.340 --> 01:03:18.750
of I'm keeping things from you.

01:03:18.750 --> 01:03:20.190
It's just that like,

01:03:20.190 --> 01:03:21.750
there's only so many hours in a day.

01:03:21.750 --> 01:03:24.060
And even though we spend the
majority of them together,

01:03:24.060 --> 01:03:26.610
we're always occupied with
the things that we're doing.

01:03:26.610 --> 01:03:28.950
Jessie asks me multiple times a week.

01:03:28.950 --> 01:03:30.060
Did you talk to Link about so-and-so?

01:03:30.060 --> 01:03:30.903
I'm like baby?

01:03:32.310 --> 01:03:35.169
No, because we talked
about every other thing,

01:03:35.169 --> 01:03:36.002
you know what I'm saying?

01:03:36.002 --> 01:03:37.260
Like.
but.

01:03:37.260 --> 01:03:39.060
Because we're constantly.

01:03:39.060 --> 01:03:40.860
I recognize all that.

01:03:40.860 --> 01:03:42.146
Yeah.

01:03:42.146 --> 01:03:43.953
But my experience with it was,

01:03:45.390 --> 01:03:49.140
it was just a little thing here,

01:03:49.140 --> 01:03:52.773
a little thing there, an EP, an album.

01:03:56.350 --> 01:03:59.933
And so I'm like without
having the full story,

01:04:01.140 --> 01:04:05.434
I think there was a lot of,
well, I'm just left to like,

01:04:05.434 --> 01:04:07.290
okay, how am I gonna respond to this?

01:04:07.290 --> 01:04:11.220
Yeah, and again, none
of that was calculated.

01:04:11.220 --> 01:04:12.930
If I think back and try to figure out

01:04:12.930 --> 01:04:15.360
why that was the way that it happened.

01:04:15.360 --> 01:04:17.400
I think there is a part of my,

01:04:17.400 --> 01:04:19.140
there's a part of me that believes,

01:04:19.140 --> 01:04:22.233
and this is just kind of
the way my brain works,

01:04:23.340 --> 01:04:26.370
Sometimes talking about something.

01:04:26.370 --> 01:04:28.860
the only thing that is good
that comes from talking about

01:04:28.860 --> 01:04:30.860
something is talking yourself out of it.

01:04:32.324 --> 01:04:34.230
And so I don't like to
talk a lot about things.

01:04:34.230 --> 01:04:36.450
I just like to keep doing them.

01:04:36.450 --> 01:04:38.994
So you're saying, if you
would've talked to me about it,

01:04:38.994 --> 01:04:41.670
you would've talked yourself out of it.

01:04:41.670 --> 01:04:43.080
I think that not, again,

01:04:43.080 --> 01:04:44.220
I haven't thought about this at all,

01:04:44.220 --> 01:04:48.210
but I think that there's a fear that like,

01:04:48.210 --> 01:04:50.463
because this doesn't make any sense,

01:04:51.541 --> 01:04:52.500
because I don't have time for this,

01:04:52.500 --> 01:04:55.863
because this is not necessarily
a good business decision.

01:04:58.680 --> 01:05:00.513
If we start talking about it,

01:05:02.429 --> 01:05:04.320
to then like talk about it
from a strategic standpoint

01:05:04.320 --> 01:05:05.970
or a positioning standpoint,

01:05:05.970 --> 01:05:08.550
it may just float away.

01:05:08.550 --> 01:05:10.500
It may just not be a priority.

01:05:10.500 --> 01:05:12.300
But for me it was like,

01:05:12.300 --> 01:05:15.307
this is a personal thing that I'm like,

01:05:15.307 --> 01:05:17.340
I'm revisiting on my own time.

01:05:17.340 --> 01:05:19.590
Up until very, very recently,

01:05:19.590 --> 01:05:21.540
I never did any of this during work hours.

01:05:21.540 --> 01:05:23.640
This past couple of months,

01:05:23.640 --> 01:05:24.990
there's been a couple of
days where I've been like,

01:05:24.990 --> 01:05:27.720
I have to go record this
or I have to do that.

01:05:27.720 --> 01:05:30.483
That's kind of gotten
into my regular schedule,

01:05:31.976 --> 01:05:33.753
but because it was very something

01:05:33.753 --> 01:05:34.800
that I just kept pushing forward

01:05:34.800 --> 01:05:38.343
in my free time, so to
speak, free time, air quotes,

01:05:39.780 --> 01:05:41.043
I think it was.

01:05:41.910 --> 01:05:43.950
There was just this unspoken.

01:05:43.950 --> 01:05:46.650
I don't wanna sit down and have
a real serious conversation

01:05:46.650 --> 01:05:48.963
about this because I
don't wanna slow it down,

01:05:50.172 --> 01:05:52.560
because it's gaining so
much momentum personally.

01:05:52.560 --> 01:05:54.750
Not that I thought that you
would talk me out of it,

01:05:54.750 --> 01:05:56.220
that's not really what I'm saying.

01:05:56.220 --> 01:05:58.980
But I hear you saying that
if we talked about it,

01:05:58.980 --> 01:06:00.843
it would very quickly get to like,

01:06:06.323 --> 01:06:07.156
what is the feasibility of this?

01:06:07.156 --> 01:06:07.989
There's not.

01:06:09.942 --> 01:06:12.592
There's not a lot of positives
to it in terms of like

01:06:13.650 --> 01:06:16.020
Mythical unless you're
really talking about,

01:06:16.020 --> 01:06:19.140
I want to do this as a
solo artist and this,

01:06:19.140 --> 01:06:21.600
if it became some Mythical endeavor

01:06:21.600 --> 01:06:22.890
from a business standpoint,

01:06:22.890 --> 01:06:27.240
there's a lot more questions
that all feel like roadblocks

01:06:27.240 --> 01:06:29.670
to this personal project if
we had that conversation.

01:06:29.670 --> 01:06:31.303
That's why I took a long time.

01:06:31.303 --> 01:06:34.260
I didn't talk to anyone here
about it for the longest time,

01:06:34.260 --> 01:06:35.100
for the same reasons.

01:06:35.100 --> 01:06:36.213
'Cause like, guys,

01:06:37.440 --> 01:06:39.630
you may interpret this as a selfish act,

01:06:39.630 --> 01:06:41.190
if I start talking about it.

01:06:41.190 --> 01:06:42.030
And you're like,

01:06:42.030 --> 01:06:43.350
we're always working so busy

01:06:43.350 --> 01:06:46.260
and you're off making your little album.

01:06:46.260 --> 01:06:47.240
So you know what I'm saying?

01:06:47.240 --> 01:06:50.613
So you didn't bring it
up because it could be,

01:06:51.960 --> 01:06:56.960
it could be perceived as like
a threat to the business.

01:06:57.030 --> 01:06:59.460
Yeah, now I firmly believe that it is not.

01:06:59.460 --> 01:07:02.260
And I have a lot of reasons
for believing that it's not.

01:07:03.402 --> 01:07:07.680
I think that the way I
kind of analyze that is,

01:07:07.680 --> 01:07:10.270
is funny because what we have

01:07:12.635 --> 01:07:13.923
is incredibly unusual.

01:07:15.390 --> 01:07:19.230
I actually can't think
of a entertainment duo

01:07:19.230 --> 01:07:22.690
where both people are
qualified entertainers

01:07:24.782 --> 01:07:26.682
and literally every expression of that

01:07:27.710 --> 01:07:28.543
is only in the context of that.

01:07:28.543 --> 01:07:31.140
Almost every duo that there's
an example of is just like,

01:07:31.140 --> 01:07:32.940
oh yeah and he does his little thing,

01:07:32.940 --> 01:07:34.500
his little side hobby thing.

01:07:34.500 --> 01:07:36.033
It's like super common, right?

01:07:37.950 --> 01:07:39.600
But the main thing they do

01:07:39.600 --> 01:07:40.770
is the stuff that they do together.

01:07:40.770 --> 01:07:44.370
I always thought that the reason that

01:07:44.370 --> 01:07:48.330
that hadn't been the case
up until now is twofold.

01:07:48.330 --> 01:07:50.340
Number one, it's like, we just
never have time for anything.

01:07:50.340 --> 01:07:52.020
And number two, it just never,

01:07:52.020 --> 01:07:54.150
I never had an idea
that it made sense to go

01:07:54.150 --> 01:07:56.430
and do by myself until this.

01:07:56.430 --> 01:08:00.000
So it isn't like I've been
sitting around thinking.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:02.744
I find it unusual that we
haven't done anything solo

01:08:02.744 --> 01:08:06.360
independently of each
other for all these years.

01:08:06.360 --> 01:08:08.430
But I also find it, it kind of makes sense

01:08:08.430 --> 01:08:11.520
because there hasn't been,

01:08:11.520 --> 01:08:13.320
neither of us have had
something where it's just like,

01:08:13.320 --> 01:08:14.820
I've gotta get this into the world.

01:08:14.820 --> 01:08:17.130
This is the first thing that came along.

01:08:17.130 --> 01:08:20.280
To me, it doesn't feel like
a threat to what we have,

01:08:20.280 --> 01:08:22.920
if anything, it feels like,

01:08:22.920 --> 01:08:25.020
because it's not a replacement of anything

01:08:25.020 --> 01:08:25.950
that we're doing.

01:08:25.950 --> 01:08:27.374
Well.

01:08:27.374 --> 01:08:30.040
In some ways it feels like another facet

01:08:32.112 --> 01:08:34.293
to the Rhett side of Rhett and Link.

01:08:35.250 --> 01:08:36.870
Do you know what I'm getting at?

01:08:36.870 --> 01:08:40.053
Yeah, I think that there
was, so it was the,

01:08:42.128 --> 01:08:45.090
was this a threat to the business strategy

01:08:45.090 --> 01:08:46.230
of what we're doing,

01:08:46.230 --> 01:08:48.180
but then there's another part that's like,

01:08:48.180 --> 01:08:49.413
if I bring this up,

01:08:53.430 --> 01:08:55.540
will Link perceive it as a threat

01:08:58.216 --> 01:08:59.616
to our creative partnership?

01:09:02.250 --> 01:09:03.333
And I thought that.

01:09:05.716 --> 01:09:07.530
Or more, or our friendship, I don't know.

01:09:07.530 --> 01:09:10.260
Well, and again, while
it wasn't calculated,

01:09:10.260 --> 01:09:12.847
if you were to ask me like,
okay, well, all right.

01:09:12.847 --> 01:09:14.220
We're gonna have to have

01:09:14.220 --> 01:09:16.837
a really long conversation about this.

01:09:16.837 --> 01:09:18.990
That is going to, again,
I didn't think this,

01:09:18.990 --> 01:09:21.300
but I may have been
thinking it subconsciously.

01:09:21.300 --> 01:09:23.010
That's just like, okay,

01:09:23.010 --> 01:09:24.093
if we have a conversation about this

01:09:24.093 --> 01:09:28.863
at a really early stage, it may
really just get bogged down.

01:09:30.390 --> 01:09:33.730
Because now in my mind,
what went from being

01:09:35.415 --> 01:09:38.130
this thing that was gaining momentum,

01:09:38.130 --> 01:09:40.200
it's so difficult to get things to happen

01:09:40.200 --> 01:09:41.670
and bring things into the world.

01:09:41.670 --> 01:09:42.723
We know that, right?

01:09:45.741 --> 01:09:48.240
And when I subconsciously
perceive that there might be

01:09:48.240 --> 01:09:50.160
a conversation or some point

01:09:50.160 --> 01:09:52.590
that becomes a point of impasse,

01:09:52.590 --> 01:09:54.480
I'm like, I don't wanna have that.

01:09:54.480 --> 01:09:55.540
I don't wanna do that.

01:09:55.540 --> 01:09:58.200
Let's this actually begin
to become something.

01:09:58.200 --> 01:10:00.210
And then we can have a
conversation about it

01:10:00.210 --> 01:10:02.660
versus having a conversation
about it a year ago.

01:10:04.500 --> 01:10:05.610
Not that we didn't talk about it.

01:10:05.610 --> 01:10:07.650
Not that you didn't know
about it, but it wasn't like,

01:10:07.650 --> 01:10:10.530
hey, let's sit down and
literally hash this thing out.

01:10:10.530 --> 01:10:12.870
'Cause in some ways the other
part of my brain was thinking,

01:10:12.870 --> 01:10:14.270
there's nothing to hash out.

01:10:15.432 --> 01:10:16.710
Like I'm doing this thing.

01:10:16.710 --> 01:10:19.950
If you were doing this thing,
I'd be like, that's awesome.

01:10:19.950 --> 01:10:21.225
That's cool, man.

01:10:21.225 --> 01:10:22.290
Do it.

01:10:22.290 --> 01:10:25.050
Now if it suddenly we can't
do something that we wanna do,

01:10:25.050 --> 01:10:27.030
'cause you're doing this, then
we can have a conversation.

01:10:27.030 --> 01:10:29.520
But if that's not the
case, just keep going.

01:10:29.520 --> 01:10:31.770
If it's making you a better,

01:10:31.770 --> 01:10:33.690
more fulfilled person, then
that makes you a better,

01:10:33.690 --> 01:10:35.610
more fulfilled comedy partner,

01:10:35.610 --> 01:10:37.800
a business partner and friend,

01:10:37.800 --> 01:10:40.500
if you're pursuing your
passion and doing something,

01:10:40.500 --> 01:10:42.930
that's bringing you joy in life.

01:10:42.930 --> 01:10:44.550
So I think that's my,

01:10:44.550 --> 01:10:45.870
that's how I feel about it.

01:10:45.870 --> 01:10:46.703
Honestly.

01:10:46.703 --> 01:10:49.080
That's why I feel like
it's a healthy thing for me

01:10:49.080 --> 01:10:51.033
and ultimately for us,

01:10:53.220 --> 01:10:55.178
because anything that's healthy for me

01:10:55.178 --> 01:10:56.850
is healthy for us and vice versa.

01:10:56.850 --> 01:10:59.010
Anything that's helpful
for you is helpful for us.

01:10:59.010 --> 01:11:01.260
Is healthy for us.

