01:23:28.710 --> 01:23:30.420
is not a part of Mythical,

01:23:30.420 --> 01:23:32.340
but the reason that it's
not a part of Mythical

01:23:32.340 --> 01:23:36.750
is because I did not
want to make anyone here,

01:23:37.650 --> 01:23:39.570
have to work on it.

01:23:39.570 --> 01:23:42.810
Cara, our personal
assistant has been helping,

01:23:42.810 --> 01:23:44.310
but beyond that,

01:23:44.310 --> 01:23:48.240
very few people have been
involved and every single expense

01:23:48.240 --> 01:23:51.660
has come outta my pocket,
which I am reasonably certain,

01:23:51.660 --> 01:23:53.760
I will not make money from this project.

01:23:53.760 --> 01:23:55.320
Yeah, you didn't want me to lose money,

01:23:55.320 --> 01:23:56.153
but then hey,

01:23:56.153 --> 01:23:58.320
if this gets wildly successful,

01:23:58.320 --> 01:24:00.900
you're probably gonna
have to cut me in somehow.

01:24:00.900 --> 01:24:01.733
We'll have to talk about it.

01:24:01.733 --> 01:24:03.605
So that's the only reason it's not.

01:24:03.605 --> 01:24:04.438
And it's also,

01:24:04.438 --> 01:24:05.730
this is not a core,

01:24:05.730 --> 01:24:07.480
a funny podcast with your dad

01:24:08.672 --> 01:24:11.770
is a part of the core,
sort of focus of Mythical,

01:24:11.770 --> 01:24:13.950
a serious country album
about deconstruction

01:24:13.950 --> 01:24:16.150
is not part of the core
mission of Mythical.

01:24:17.471 --> 01:24:18.304
So there's a number of reasons

01:24:18.304 --> 01:24:19.710
that it's not a mythical thing.

01:24:19.710 --> 01:24:22.320
And that also is one of the
reasons that I don't really work

01:24:22.320 --> 01:24:25.290
on it here or with the
people at this company

01:24:25.290 --> 01:24:28.623
and I work on it outside of my
normal responsibilities here.

01:24:29.940 --> 01:24:32.953
But we're at a point in our career

01:24:32.953 --> 01:24:33.786
when we can do things that

01:24:33.786 --> 01:24:35.973
are associated with our careers,

01:24:37.732 --> 01:24:39.600
that don't involve the other person,

01:24:39.600 --> 01:24:41.850
but will be a part of Mythical.

01:24:41.850 --> 01:24:43.260
Of course.

01:24:43.260 --> 01:24:45.130
So Dispatches from Myrtle Beach

01:24:47.741 --> 01:24:48.750
is a great example of that.

01:24:48.750 --> 01:24:49.713
Yeah, and I mean.

01:24:50.760 --> 01:24:52.852
There may be other things.

01:24:52.852 --> 01:24:54.302
There should be other things.

01:24:55.213 --> 01:24:56.280
So one of the things we
haven't talked about,

01:24:56.280 --> 01:24:58.880
I know we're going a little
bit long, but it's fine.

01:25:02.849 --> 01:25:04.380
I think that there, I mean,

01:25:04.380 --> 01:25:06.491
I'm interested how you feel

01:25:06.491 --> 01:25:07.980
about Dispatches from Myrtle Beach

01:25:07.980 --> 01:25:11.160
in regards to this,
because one of the things,

01:25:11.160 --> 01:25:12.630
first of all,

01:25:12.630 --> 01:25:14.740
I get so creatively frustrated

01:25:15.870 --> 01:25:18.750
because as much as we
put out into the world,

01:25:18.750 --> 01:25:21.870
there's a lot more that doesn't
make it out into the world

01:25:21.870 --> 01:25:23.403
because of limitations,

01:25:25.089 --> 01:25:27.833
because we're conceptualizing things

01:25:27.833 --> 01:25:29.190
that need to be green lit by people

01:25:29.190 --> 01:25:31.200
and they need to be
financed and they have to go

01:25:31.200 --> 01:25:33.928
through pitch meetings,
etcetera, etcetera.

01:25:33.928 --> 01:25:35.940
And some of the ideas
that I'm most passionate

01:25:35.940 --> 01:25:38.950
about that I feel are most representative

01:25:40.040 --> 01:25:41.850
of us creatively are things

01:25:41.850 --> 01:25:44.730
that we can't just put
out on YouTube for free.

01:25:44.730 --> 01:25:47.330
They have to be financed
and it's a different model.

01:25:49.103 --> 01:25:51.153
And very few of those things have made it

01:25:52.585 --> 01:25:54.480
to where people can enjoy them.

01:25:54.480 --> 01:25:55.646
Yeah.

01:25:55.646 --> 01:25:57.071
With music.

01:25:57.071 --> 01:25:58.920
No one else, like if
I can get somebody to,

01:25:58.920 --> 01:26:00.960
I don't even have to get
somebody to produce it.

01:26:00.960 --> 01:26:02.360
Like I could just record it,

01:26:03.777 --> 01:26:05.393
at the Creative House and release it.

01:26:06.751 --> 01:26:09.103
You can just go through Spotify or what,

01:26:09.103 --> 01:26:10.920
you just distribute your music.

01:26:10.920 --> 01:26:15.900
There's been something so
freeing and life giving in just

01:26:15.900 --> 01:26:18.180
something happening, like having an idea.

01:26:18.180 --> 01:26:21.603
And then it can just be
birthed and given to the world.

01:26:22.650 --> 01:26:24.450
But part of that has been.

01:26:24.450 --> 01:26:25.323
And, yep.

01:26:26.306 --> 01:26:27.506
Doing it independently

01:26:29.344 --> 01:26:30.177
and it not being a collaborative thing.

01:26:30.177 --> 01:26:33.062
To me there's been,

01:26:33.062 --> 01:26:38.062
it's made me appreciate the
things that are collaborative.

01:26:40.170 --> 01:26:44.160
And I've also just, hey, this is on me.

01:26:44.160 --> 01:26:45.660
I gotta finish this.

01:26:45.660 --> 01:26:47.910
I have to be the one to make the call.

01:26:47.910 --> 01:26:51.120
I've got to make these
decisions and move this forward.

01:26:51.120 --> 01:26:53.250
And then also like do a bunch of things

01:26:53.250 --> 01:26:56.220
that I haven't done in years.

01:26:56.220 --> 01:26:59.740
Like I designed the artwork

01:27:01.697 --> 01:27:02.966
for the first single.

01:27:02.966 --> 01:27:03.799
I don't design artwork.

01:27:03.799 --> 01:27:04.710
Yeah, I was very surprised.

01:27:04.710 --> 01:27:07.890
But I was like, I don't
wanna pay somebody else.

01:27:07.890 --> 01:27:10.860
I'm paying so many people
to do so many parts of this.

01:27:10.860 --> 01:27:12.210
I don't wanna pay
somebody else to do this.

01:27:12.210 --> 01:27:14.220
It feels like I can figure this out,

01:27:14.220 --> 01:27:16.270
but there's been something very rewarding

01:27:17.302 --> 01:27:18.210
about just conceptualizing

01:27:18.210 --> 01:27:19.950
and executing something and putting it

01:27:19.950 --> 01:27:22.440
on into the world on my own.

01:27:22.440 --> 01:27:24.620
I haven't done that in so long.

01:27:24.620 --> 01:27:25.453
Yeah.

01:27:25.453 --> 01:27:28.140
There's been something personally
rewarding in doing that.

01:27:28.140 --> 01:27:29.100
Not because it's like, oh,

01:27:29.100 --> 01:27:30.578
finally I get to do something on my own.

01:27:30.578 --> 01:27:31.637
It's just like,

01:27:31.637 --> 01:27:35.562
oh no, I made a decision
to do this on my own.

01:27:35.562 --> 01:27:37.050
And it's been life giving

01:27:37.050 --> 01:27:39.690
in a different way than a collaboration.

01:27:39.690 --> 01:27:41.280
Yeah.

01:27:41.280 --> 01:27:46.280
I think that fans of ours,
Mythical Beasts will ask.

01:27:48.090 --> 01:27:49.680
Yeah, but I mean, why?

01:27:49.680 --> 01:27:52.920
There's backup, there's harmony.

01:27:52.920 --> 01:27:54.990
Why didn't you get him to sing some,

01:27:54.990 --> 01:27:58.197
why didn't you get sing some
harmony on that, you know?

01:27:58.197 --> 01:28:01.830
And that was very specifically
a calculated decision.

01:28:01.830 --> 01:28:02.793
Talk about that.

01:28:03.870 --> 01:28:05.023
Because.

01:28:05.023 --> 01:28:06.053
'Cause we haven't talked about that,

01:28:06.972 --> 01:28:08.400
but I I'm reading between the lines and I.

01:28:08.400 --> 01:28:13.290
Yeah, because when I sing
melody and you sing harmony,

01:28:13.290 --> 01:28:15.300
that's a Rhett and Link song.

01:28:15.300 --> 01:28:17.640
that's a Rhett and Link song.

01:28:17.640 --> 01:28:20.070
This isn't a Rhett and Link project.

01:28:20.070 --> 01:28:23.340
And I don't want people to think,

01:28:23.340 --> 01:28:27.360
it needs to be its own thing, right?

01:28:27.360 --> 01:28:28.470
It doesn't need to be like,

01:28:28.470 --> 01:28:30.660
oh, Rhett and Link also
made a country album.

01:28:30.660 --> 01:28:31.493
Right.

01:28:31.493 --> 01:28:32.326
No, no, no.

01:28:32.326 --> 01:28:33.159
It's just not a Rhett and Link thing.

01:28:33.159 --> 01:28:33.992
It's a Rhett thing.

01:28:33.992 --> 01:28:35.695
And that's okay.

01:28:35.695 --> 01:28:36.528
And you know what?

01:28:36.528 --> 01:28:38.673
It's good is what I'm saying.

01:28:40.170 --> 01:28:41.970
Sure, you would've been great at it.

01:28:44.550 --> 01:28:45.663
I think that, but I,

01:28:48.733 --> 01:28:50.190
but even from a Sonic's standpoint,

01:28:50.190 --> 01:28:52.440
I want it to feel like its own thing.

01:28:52.440 --> 01:28:55.020
Me and you singing together
is a very specific,

01:28:55.020 --> 01:28:56.640
great and beautiful thing.

01:28:56.640 --> 01:28:58.290
But it's a Rhett and Link thing.

01:28:58.290 --> 01:29:00.240
I don't wanna take the
Rhett and Link thing

01:29:00.240 --> 01:29:02.430
and spread it over into this,

01:29:02.430 --> 01:29:03.900
that cheapens the Rhett and Link thing.

01:29:03.900 --> 01:29:06.813
And it cheapens the James and
the Shame thing, you know?

01:29:08.949 --> 01:29:10.710
And so I want this to
have a signature sound.

01:29:10.710 --> 01:29:12.660
So like in that song that
we listened to today,

01:29:12.660 --> 01:29:13.620
that's Derek singing.

01:29:13.620 --> 01:29:15.960
He's great vocalist.

01:29:15.960 --> 01:29:18.870
That's him singing the backup lyrics.

01:29:18.870 --> 01:29:21.510
But there are songs where
I sing my own harmony,

01:29:21.510 --> 01:29:23.790
when it makes sense thematically.

01:29:23.790 --> 01:29:27.315
There are songs were Jessie sings harmony,

01:29:27.315 --> 01:29:28.583
where it makes sense thematically.

01:29:32.117 --> 01:29:33.191
But the thing that did,

01:29:33.191 --> 01:29:35.100
if I had a song about you on the album,

01:29:35.100 --> 01:29:36.261
then it would make sense for,

01:29:36.261 --> 01:29:37.163
you know what I'm saying?

01:29:37.163 --> 01:29:38.700
Then it would make sense for you

01:29:38.700 --> 01:29:40.319
to sing the song.

01:29:40.319 --> 01:29:42.033
It was like the, to me,

01:29:43.048 --> 01:29:43.881
it was about theme.

01:29:43.881 --> 01:29:45.780
Unless it's about me being dead.

01:29:45.780 --> 01:29:47.490
And standing on its own.

01:29:47.490 --> 01:29:48.783
And it was like, hey,

01:29:52.109 --> 01:29:55.020
at one point it became
almost out of principle.

01:29:55.020 --> 01:29:58.780
Like, I don't want Link to
hear this until it's done

01:30:02.498 --> 01:30:04.320
because it's not a Rhett and
Link thing, not outta spite,

01:30:04.320 --> 01:30:06.570
but because of all the reasons
that we've just covered.

01:30:06.570 --> 01:30:08.280
And it's like, I don't
wanna complicate that.

01:30:08.280 --> 01:30:10.350
I don't wanna complicate
that and muddy that.

01:30:10.350 --> 01:30:12.420
If it really is Rhett thing,

01:30:12.420 --> 01:30:13.820
then let it be a Rhett thing

01:30:14.975 --> 01:30:15.808
and something that then I can just

01:30:15.808 --> 01:30:18.420
kind of present to you and you can enjoy.

01:30:18.420 --> 01:30:20.070
And honestly, I've been treating

01:30:20.070 --> 01:30:21.960
Dispatches from Myrtle
Beach the exact same way.

01:30:21.960 --> 01:30:22.793
Like I haven't,

01:30:25.332 --> 01:30:26.460
I am at the time that
we're recording this,

01:30:26.460 --> 01:30:28.290
the first episode's about to drop.

01:30:28.290 --> 01:30:30.540
And that's when I'm gonna
listen to it for the first time,

01:30:30.540 --> 01:30:33.750
I'm gonna listen to it as a fan

01:30:33.750 --> 01:30:36.060
of listening to you and your dad talk,

01:30:36.060 --> 01:30:38.910
not as somebody who's a
producer and it's gonna be like,

01:30:38.910 --> 01:30:41.110
well, let me give you
some feedback on that.

01:30:42.299 --> 01:30:43.132
Do you know what I'm saying?

01:30:43.132 --> 01:30:44.006
Yeah.

01:30:44.006 --> 01:30:45.669
And to me, there's something healthy

01:30:45.669 --> 01:30:46.769
about that separation.

01:30:47.687 --> 01:30:49.983
I respect that, I understand that.

01:30:52.230 --> 01:30:54.630
Is there anything else
that you wanted to share?

01:30:58.380 --> 01:30:59.280
I don't think so.

01:30:59.280 --> 01:31:02.200
Obviously, I'll use this time to say

01:31:03.425 --> 01:31:04.925
that I am genuinely interested

01:31:06.057 --> 01:31:07.657
in a lot of people hearing this.

01:31:09.120 --> 01:31:11.490
And so it gets to the people
who it will impact in the way

01:31:11.490 --> 01:31:13.440
that I would like to see them impacted.

01:31:16.431 --> 01:31:18.540
So do all the things that
you do with the musicians

01:31:18.540 --> 01:31:20.853
that you like, you know?

01:31:21.905 --> 01:31:25.320
Listen to it, follow me on those places.

01:31:25.320 --> 01:31:27.030
I am creating, like.

01:31:27.030 --> 01:31:30.150
I think you should refer
to it in the third person.

01:31:30.150 --> 01:31:33.739
I'm creating James and the Shame profiles

01:31:33.739 --> 01:31:34.950
in different places, but
only as placeholders.

01:31:34.950 --> 01:31:36.390
So people don't steal them,

01:31:36.390 --> 01:31:38.970
but all updates about this are gonna come

01:31:38.970 --> 01:31:41.010
through all my initial social channels.

01:31:41.010 --> 01:31:43.950
So you can go like follow those place,

01:31:43.950 --> 01:31:45.180
those accounts over there,

01:31:45.180 --> 01:31:47.340
just so that somebody
will be following them,

01:31:47.340 --> 01:31:50.290
but it's primarily gonna just
be done through all my stuff.

01:31:52.901 --> 01:31:55.920
But I would like, it would do nothing.

01:31:55.920 --> 01:31:57.060
It would do my heart very,

01:31:57.060 --> 01:32:00.720
very well for somebody out
there who likes this kind.

01:32:00.720 --> 01:32:03.750
The only reason they're
listening to what I'm doing

01:32:03.750 --> 01:32:06.630
is because they like the music.

01:32:06.630 --> 01:32:08.184
And then they're like,

01:32:08.184 --> 01:32:10.320
this guy's not singing about the stuff

01:32:10.320 --> 01:32:13.770
that I typically listen
to in country music.

01:32:13.770 --> 01:32:16.500
This guy seems to be challenging.

01:32:16.500 --> 01:32:19.980
It would be cool if it
developed a life of its own.

01:32:19.980 --> 01:32:20.813
Yeah.

01:32:22.100 --> 01:32:23.400
And that again is,

01:32:23.400 --> 01:32:25.510
that's my desire is that this thing

01:32:26.430 --> 01:32:31.430
has a home in people who
will relate to the story

01:32:32.922 --> 01:32:34.158
that I'm telling.

01:32:34.158 --> 01:32:35.463
And so if you think you
know somebody who is like,

01:32:35.463 --> 01:32:37.980
I've never sent anything to this person,

01:32:37.980 --> 01:32:39.960
because I know they're not
gonna like X, Y, and Z,

01:32:39.960 --> 01:32:40.793
that these guys have done.

01:32:40.793 --> 01:32:44.040
If you're like, oh, they might
like this, send it to 'em.

01:32:44.040 --> 01:32:45.540
So that's what I would
ask the Mystical Beasts

01:32:45.540 --> 01:32:47.730
is just like, give it a chance.

01:32:47.730 --> 01:32:48.870
Don't see it as a threat.

01:32:48.870 --> 01:32:51.600
Hopefully what we've talked about today,

01:32:51.600 --> 01:32:53.659
if that was your concern,

01:32:53.659 --> 01:32:55.559
that you understand that this is about

01:32:57.060 --> 01:33:00.853
personal expression and
ultimately a healthy thing

01:33:00.853 --> 01:33:02.580
that is not a existential threat

01:33:02.580 --> 01:33:05.070
to Mythical or anything Rhett and Link,

01:33:05.070 --> 01:33:07.670
if anything an enhancement
to what we're doing here,

01:33:10.713 --> 01:33:13.830
but also share it with people
who you think might like it.

01:33:13.830 --> 01:33:14.850
That's all I'll say.

01:33:14.850 --> 01:33:16.410
Awesome.

01:33:16.410 --> 01:33:19.802
Alright, I think you're
supposed to have a rec.

01:33:19.802 --> 01:33:20.790
Are you recking your own single?

01:33:20.790 --> 01:33:21.623
Man, I can't.

01:33:21.623 --> 01:33:22.456
It seems like you kinda have to.

01:33:22.456 --> 01:33:23.888
Just do it.

01:33:23.888 --> 01:33:25.072
Just rec your own single.

01:33:25.072 --> 01:33:26.190
Yeah, I recommend that you go over.

01:33:26.190 --> 01:33:27.060
What's it called?

01:33:27.060 --> 01:33:28.263
It's called, Believe Me.

01:33:29.130 --> 01:33:31.346
And at some point,

01:33:31.346 --> 01:33:32.760
hey, I am gonna have,

01:33:32.760 --> 01:33:34.950
there's gonna be some
James and the Shame merch.

01:33:34.950 --> 01:33:36.060
I don't know if that'll be the case

01:33:36.060 --> 01:33:37.389
by the time this goes up.

01:33:37.389 --> 01:33:38.580
Nipple clamps?

01:33:38.580 --> 01:33:41.229
There's gonna be some of that as well.

01:33:41.229 --> 01:33:42.579
So you can spread the word.

01:33:43.830 --> 01:33:44.663
G strings?

01:33:44.663 --> 01:33:45.496
I'll just say,

01:33:45.496 --> 01:33:47.700
just follow me where
you listen to your music

01:33:47.700 --> 01:33:51.120
and listen, put it in a playlist,

01:33:51.120 --> 01:33:53.013
whatever you do with music.

01:33:54.270 --> 01:33:55.323
Alright.

01:33:56.250 --> 01:33:59.411
Next week, we'll talk at you.

01:33:59.411 --> 01:34:00.244
#earbiscuits.

01:34:00.244 --> 01:34:01.518
Hi, Rhett and Link.

01:34:01.518 --> 01:34:03.900
I was just listening to the
podcast where you're discussing

01:34:03.900 --> 01:34:05.800
keeping the shower curtain open

01:34:06.964 --> 01:34:07.797
or closed when you're done with it.

01:34:07.797 --> 01:34:11.260
I'm very passionate about
keeping the shower curtain open

01:34:12.985 --> 01:34:15.300
because I don't want a serial
killer to be hiding behind it.

01:34:15.300 --> 01:34:16.380
Just thought I'd mention it.

01:34:16.380 --> 01:34:18.758
'Cause I didn't know the default

01:34:18.758 --> 01:34:19.890
was to keep it close all the time.

01:34:19.890 --> 01:34:20.910
So I'm here to say,

01:34:20.910 --> 01:34:22.650
keep your shower curtains open

01:34:22.650 --> 01:34:25.590
so that there's no serial
killers, thank you, bye.

01:34:25.590 --> 01:34:26.820
Hi, Rhett and Link.

01:34:26.820 --> 01:34:28.050
My name is Molly.

01:34:28.050 --> 01:34:30.780
I just wanted to let you guys
know that I just had dental

01:34:30.780 --> 01:34:33.900
surgery and was listening to your podcast

01:34:33.900 --> 01:34:36.570
while I was breathing
in the nitrous oxide.

01:34:36.570 --> 01:34:38.010
And for a couple minutes there,

01:34:38.010 --> 01:34:42.670
I transformed myself into
the table of dim lighting

01:34:43.809 --> 01:34:46.410
and I saw you two and also Stevie.

01:34:46.410 --> 01:34:48.360
So it was a very weird experience,

01:34:48.360 --> 01:34:50.100
but I'm very grateful for it.

01:34:50.100 --> 01:34:52.470
You guys got me through
the surgery, so thanks.

01:34:52.470 --> 01:34:54.090
Hey Rhett, hey Link.

01:34:54.090 --> 01:34:55.843
